00:00:07,104 --> 00:00:15,985
Question twelve: answer C. In binary one zero one one zero one, the third one-bit from the right has place value two to the three.

3
00:00:15,985 --> 00:00:23,840
Question thirteen: answer C. Minus fifty-three in eight-bit two's complement is one one zero zero one zero one one.

4
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:29,715
Steps: write fifty-three as zero zero one one zero one zero one; invert, then add one.

5
00:00:29,715 --> 00:00:35,248
Question fourteen: answer A. Hello — five characters, one byte each — five bytes.

6
00:00:35,248 --> 00:00:43,992
Question fifteen: answer B. Even parity: five ones in the data bits — odd — so set the parity bit to one to make the total even.

